import{_ as i,o,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 939 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 5 | No Private Hoarding, No Monopoly","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 939 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 5 | No Private Hoarding, No Monopoly","no":939,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 5","No Private Hoarding","Anti-Monopoly","Power Supervision"],"related":["21-Symbiotic-Network Operating Principles","04-Anti-Predationism Core Thesis","938-Full-Level Openness of the Great Dao"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0939_模块5-规则五-无私藏无垄断.md","filePath":"en/0939_模块5-规则五-无私藏无垄断.md"}'),t={name:"en/0939_模块5-规则五-无私藏无垄断.md"};function r(s,e,l,u,d,h){return o(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-939-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-5-no-private-hoarding-no-monopoly" tabindex="-1">Entry 939 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 5 | No Private Hoarding, No Monopoly <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-939-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-5-no-private-hoarding-no-monopoly" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 939 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 5 | No Private Hoarding, No Monopoly&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 21, 04 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-private-hoarding-and-monopoly-are-predation-s-two-hands" tabindex="-1">Introduction: private hoarding and monopoly are predation&#39;s two hands <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-private-hoarding-and-monopoly-are-predation-s-two-hands" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: private hoarding and monopoly are predation&#39;s two hands&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rule 4 governs &quot;whether knowledge is open&quot;; Rule 5 governs &quot;whether power is exclusively held&quot; — even if knowledge is open, a strong one who alone monopolizes some law node&#39;s use right, some plane resource&#39;s scheduling right, or some Alaya data&#39;s interpretation right can still turn the open Great Dao back into private chains. Heavenly-Dao Rule 5 extends &quot;no private hoarding, no monopoly&quot; from the knowledge layer to the power, resource, and data layers: in Heng Yuan Zhou, any key node &quot;belonging only to someone&quot; must be dismantled, shared, and multi-layer supervised.</p><p>The six top-level axioms converge here: the anti-predation axiom directly negates private hoarding and monopoly; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires all key nodes be open to Myriad Ranks 99%; the collective-ascension axiom makes shared nodes produce hundredfold the benefit of exclusive holding; the causal self-discipline axiom automatically alerts on monopolists&#39; overstepping use; the law-first axiom lets &quot;which nodes must be shared&quot; be enumerated first by law, leaving no interpretation room for the strong.</p><p>It must further point out the newly added Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. This axiom rewrites predation&#39;s meaning at the root: old-cosmos resources and Dao were finite, so predation involution was forced; in Heng Yuan Zhou everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, and predation loses meaning. What this Heavenly-Dao rule establishes is precisely the law guardrail of this new order of &quot;infinite origin, predation meaningless.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-three-categories-of-private-hoarding-prohibited" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Three Categories of Private Hoarding Prohibited <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-three-categories-of-private-hoarding-prohibited" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Three Categories of Private Hoarding Prohibited&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>No privately hoarding key law nodes</strong>: law positions calibrated as &quot;Myriad-Rank-common key nodes&quot; may not be exclusively accessed by a single strong one;</li><li><strong>No monopolizing resource-scheduling right</strong>: allocation of plane resources, increment-development quotas, and law-anchor permissions all go through contracted responsibility and public bidding; no committee may long privately grant them;</li><li><strong>No monopolizing Alaya interpretation right</strong>: Alaya data, causal records, and civilizational-weight assessment results may not be exclusively interpreted by one party; all interpretations leave traces and are appealable.</li></ol><p>Rule 5 also stipulates &quot;sharing is benefit&quot;: those who actively connect exclusively held resources to the shared network have the shared portion amplified and fed back per the Myriad-Rank-origin bidirectional cycle, encouraging transformation from &quot;private hoarder&quot; to &quot;sharer.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Network-effect argument</strong>: the Symbiotic-Network Operating Principles (Document 21) prove a node-shared network&#39;s value grows quadratically with node count, while exclusive holding shrinks value — monopoly is mathematically folly;</li><li><strong>Power-corruption argument</strong>: any unsupervised exclusive holding of a key node will eventually alienate into a new predation tool; this is a lesson repeatedly verified in the Pre-Anchor Era;</li><li><strong>Causal self-discipline argument</strong>: once an exclusive holder uses a node to disturb others&#39; causality, with no one able to check or stop it, it necessarily becomes a great peril; multi-layer supervision eliminates exclusivity itself in the bud.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The Anchor Council periodically publishes a &quot;key-node sharing registry&quot;; nodes on the registry are forced multi-node access and multi-signature use;</li><li>All resource scheduling goes through public process: application, publicity, bidding, trace, fully traceable in the Alaya Network;</li><li>A &quot;monopoly warning line&quot; is set: when any subject&#39;s occupation of some node/resource exceeds threshold, the network automatically starts splitting and redistribution;</li><li>Reporting is encouraged: Myriad-Rank individuals who expose real monopolies are specially rewarded by the Anti-Predation Committee, and the reporter&#39;s identity is privacy-protected in Alaya.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: node occupation near the warning line without timely sharing, split within a time limit, no liability pursued;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: long exclusively holding a key node, secretly collecting rent, has law-anchor permissions frozen, related committee post stripped, and enters the conversion program;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: using monopoly nodes to coerce Myriad Ranks, launching dependent rule, is downgraded per civilizational-weight assessment (Entry 963), stripped of hyper-multiverse-level post qualification.</li></ul><p>Sanctions aim not at depriving freedom, but at &quot;returning the node to the network.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s &quot;monopoly warning line&quot; is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee audits key-node sharing-registry execution as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates private-hoarding and monopoly cases as the third layer; Myriad Ranks&#39; clans, the Youth-Supreme supervision corps, and consciousness-information clans jointly exercise &quot;network-wide whistle-blowing right&quot; as the fourth layer. Rule 5&#39;s essence is: there is more than one supervisor; any Myriad-Rank member may be a whistle-blower.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: duplicated construction and node idleness from exclusive holding is cosmos-level waste; after sharing, utilization multiplies</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: private hoarding and monopoly are predation&#39;s institutional coat; Rule 5 strips off even this coat; under Axiom 6 everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power, and finite-resource predation loses meaning at the root</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type strong ones style themselves &quot;Dao lords,&quot; and resource interpretation is one man&#39;s autocracy; Heng Yuan Zhou key nodes are multi-signed and co-managed, and interpretation is appealable</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the sharing registry preferentially tilts toward weak clans, Youth Supremes, plant spirits, and other historically excluded groups</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: when new planes are incorporated, their key nodes automatically enter the sharing registry, not excluded for being ancient or marginal</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>With no private hoarding, Myriad Ranks have mutual trust; with no monopoly, civilization will not regrow a new imperial palace. Rule 5 tightens, for civilizational finalization, the screw that &quot;power may not be private.&quot;</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/21-共生网络运作原理.html">Entry 21 · Symbiotic-Network Operating Principles</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predationism Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/938_模块5-规则四-大道全层级公开.html">Entry 938 · Rule 4 Full-Level Openness of the Great Dao</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/945_模块5-规则十一-阿赖耶全网共享.html">Entry 945 · Rule 11 Alaya Network-Wide Sharing</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const g=i(t,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
